  "id": "sexual-inhibition",
  "term": "sexual inhibition",
  "definition": "Sexual inhibition is the part of sexual regulation that restrains or controls sexual responses and behavior. In the source, it is described as involving both motivational and cognitive forms of inhibition and as varying across individuals alongside sexual excitation.",
